WEBVTT

00:01.400 --> 00:03.320
Letters from the departed.

00:03.940 --> 00:06.030
They're called, "Shigofumi".

00:07.320 --> 00:11.620
What qualifies someone to send
Shigofumis is strength of sentiment.

00:12.660 --> 00:14.410
The strength of love.

00:14.410 --> 00:16.160
The strength of faith.

00:16.790 --> 00:18.160
And...

00:19.920 --> 00:21.210
Hatred.

00:27.470 --> 00:27.720
The true forms

00:29.300 --> 00:29.550
Of the things that I gazed at

00:31.180 --> 00:31.430
Were for showing after I closed my eyes

00:34.890 --> 00:35.140
Again today, time

00:36.720 --> 00:36.980
Will only construct a loneliness

00:38.520 --> 00:38.770
That seems to be torn apart, right?

00:45.940 --> 00:46.190
There are people who can't forget about

00:49.610 --> 00:49.860
The white lotuses that bloom in the darkness

00:53.240 --> 00:53.490
Nevertheless, recollections

00:57.000 --> 00:57.250
Visit from the future

01:00.670 --> 01:00.920
Words that turn into sighs

01:08.090 --> 01:08.340
Are the emerging wings of the soul

01:11.760 --> 01:12.010
Will I flutter apart?

01:15.470 --> 01:15.720
Growing confused and disordered

01:19.140 --> 01:19.390
I want to carve

01:21.480 --> 01:21.730
These letters to you

01:26.480 --> 01:26.730
Pieces of the truth

01:28.320 --> 01:28.570
Of things that I want to tell you-

01:30.190 --> 01:30.450
I can't even send them well to you

01:33.950 --> 01:34.200
If I write them with the blood that stains my fingertips

01:37.620 --> 01:37.870
Then can they spill into your heart?

01:41.290 --> 01:41.540
Even if the one word left behind

01:44.540 --> 01:44.790
To us who live

01:44.790 --> 01:45.000
No

01:47.210 --> 01:47.460
Is to be goodbye

01:47.460 --> 01:47.800
Sa

01:56.510 --> 01:57.930
Fumika, let's get out of here!

01:58.260 --> 02:01.230
She's not normal.

02:02.390 --> 02:03.440
No, she's normal.

02:03.440 --> 02:04.310
Eh?

02:04.310 --> 02:06.230
She has something important to her.

02:06.230 --> 02:07.820
Something is getting in her way.

02:07.820 --> 02:09.650
That's something normal.

02:09.650 --> 02:13.530
What are you saying, Fumika?
She killed someone! She's a murderer!

02:13.860 --> 02:16.120
I am not the judge.

02:16.120 --> 02:19.240
There is something I have to ascertain.

02:21.200 --> 02:24.210
Is Machiya Shouta your lover?

02:26.790 --> 02:28.210
Answer me.

02:28.210 --> 02:30.050
Do you have a lover?

02:30.050 --> 02:31.050
Or don't you?

02:33.590 --> 02:35.930
I have plenty of men.

02:36.220 --> 02:37.220
Understood.

02:37.220 --> 02:38.260
Fumika!

02:39.600 --> 02:41.020
0913.

03:35.860 --> 03:38.820
I wonder what will become of this place.

03:38.820 --> 03:40.580
Nothing.

03:40.580 --> 03:41.740
It will remain as is.

03:42.990 --> 03:45.080
Fumika, are you angry?

03:45.080 --> 03:46.250
No.

03:46.250 --> 03:48.460
The Gospel department made you do it, didn't they?

03:48.460 --> 03:50.920
Most likely, it was Gandolf's idea.

03:52.710 --> 03:56.420
I never imagined that that Shigofumi would have such a message.

03:56.880 --> 04:00.680
What a despicable way to use the Shigofumi.

04:01.140 --> 04:02.890
And he's the father too.

04:04.140 --> 04:06.020
That's a Shigofumi too.

04:06.480 --> 04:10.480
Irrational hatred and empty sadness.

04:10.480 --> 04:13.360
The pure-hearted possess all those.

04:16.990 --> 04:18.700
0609.

04:29.000 --> 04:32.460
Is this okay? Normally, you would look for the recipient.

04:32.460 --> 04:36.670
Shouldn't we ask around to find Ayase Asuna's lover?

04:37.220 --> 04:40.180
Men do not equate to lovers.

04:40.180 --> 04:41.390
Oh?

04:47.350 --> 04:52.480
Say, Fumika. Why do you think she murdered her own father?

04:52.480 --> 04:55.860
The reason was written inside the Shigofumi, wasn't it?

04:56.440 --> 04:59.150
That's not related to our work.

04:59.150 --> 05:01.360
But, aren't you curious?

05:01.360 --> 05:04.700
She murdered her own father and all!

05:15.960 --> 05:17.630
That's not the case.

06:08.180 --> 06:11.020
How are the Ayases doing?

06:11.020 --> 06:14.400
The younger sister, Miku, is rather shy of people.

06:25.160 --> 06:26.160
Miku.

06:28.910 --> 06:30.950
You caught it!

06:30.950 --> 06:32.410
What shall we do?

06:33.660 --> 06:34.920
Run!

06:41.420 --> 06:45.430
The sister sure takes good care of Miku-chan.

06:45.430 --> 06:46.760
She's a good girl.

06:47.300 --> 06:51.930
Because the father wasn't a very good parent.

06:52.520 --> 06:53.850
Really?

06:54.140 --> 06:58.230
I don't wish to speak ill of the dead.

06:58.230 --> 07:00.610
But he was evidently quite temperamental.

07:01.110 --> 07:04.650
This case will surely end in tragedy.

07:25.510 --> 07:27.300
Here she comes.

07:28.300 --> 07:30.050
Part-time jobs
are against the rules!!

07:28.300 --> 07:30.050
SEX MODEL

07:28.300 --> 07:30.050
Thriving business

08:13.890 --> 08:16.930
Father, I'd like to take tomorrow off.

08:16.930 --> 08:17.890
Dumbass.

08:18.690 --> 08:21.730
Do you think we have that kind of luxury?

08:22.020 --> 08:24.980
Did you get a boyfriend or something?

08:26.030 --> 08:27.070
No.

08:28.030 --> 08:30.160
I don't need you fooling around.

08:30.160 --> 08:31.950
Just think about your work.

08:32.700 --> 08:35.290
My medical fees aren't cheap after all.

08:35.290 --> 08:37.460
I'm going to ask Miku to help out tomorrow.

08:37.460 --> 08:37.960
Eh?

08:38.250 --> 08:40.880
That was the request I got earlier.

08:40.880 --> 08:42.710
Model negotiations.

08:43.170 --> 08:45.550
Oh, here it comes.

08:46.510 --> 08:49.340
Ah, his conditions are very favourable.

08:49.840 --> 08:51.720
The negotiations are complete.

08:52.390 --> 08:55.720
Am I not enough?

08:56.600 --> 08:57.270
Father...

08:57.270 --> 08:58.180
Of course not.

08:58.600 --> 09:02.310
Raising the two of you is costly.

09:02.310 --> 09:04.690
I'm in this state because of you two.

09:04.690 --> 09:07.190
It's only natural to reciprocate my kindness.

09:07.650 --> 09:08.610
Father...

09:08.610 --> 09:10.780
Shut the hell up! I'm in the middle of-

09:20.160 --> 09:21.420
Sis...

09:23.130 --> 09:25.250
W-What is it?

09:26.500 --> 09:28.260
You can't sleep?

09:29.720 --> 09:32.380
Do you want to sleep together?

09:42.190 --> 09:43.730
It'll be okay.

09:44.810 --> 09:47.480
Thanks for your concern.

09:48.650 --> 09:50.030
Sis...

09:53.320 --> 09:54.780
I love you.

09:57.160 --> 09:58.990
I protected her.

09:59.540 --> 10:00.540
I protected Miku.

10:00.960 --> 10:03.370
And her future.

10:09.760 --> 10:11.590
A lot of cops just arrived.

10:11.590 --> 10:13.470
A corpse? Seriously?

10:25.770 --> 10:28.360
Can we wait inside?

10:28.360 --> 10:29.070
Yeah.

10:29.400 --> 10:31.360
I don't mind.

10:31.360 --> 10:34.110
But, is this related to the father's case?

10:34.110 --> 10:36.450
No, this is a different one altogether.

10:36.740 --> 10:40.790
Have you ever heard about a boy
named Machiya Shouta from Asuna-san?

10:47.380 --> 10:51.710
How do they know about my
relationship with Shouta? I didn't tell anyone.

10:51.710 --> 10:52.970
Were we seen together?

10:54.220 --> 10:57.340
I got it, Dad. I'll be home soon.

10:57.340 --> 10:58.300
See you.

11:06.560 --> 11:09.940
I have to erase my existence.

11:20.740 --> 11:22.540
<i>Silver Arrow for Aomori.</i>

11:23.290 --> 11:31.090
<i>The train will stop at Omiya, Koriyama, Fukushima, Sendai, Morioka.</i>

11:33.340 --> 11:34.800
Centre
(Miku)

11:35.880 --> 11:37.380
I can't call her now.

11:38.390 --> 11:40.640
Miku, forgive me.

11:41.720 --> 11:44.310
Ah-hah! Found you!

11:47.730 --> 11:51.650
I have a delivery for you.

11:52.110 --> 11:54.110
Shigofumi

11:55.190 --> 11:57.200
Shigofumi

11:57.490 --> 12:01.870
I wonder why criminals flee northwards?

12:01.870 --> 12:04.040
I'd definitely go south.

12:04.370 --> 12:06.460
Warmer places seem more fun after all.

12:06.460 --> 12:07.580
South, south!

12:09.040 --> 12:12.500
So, it really wasn't a dream.

12:12.800 --> 12:14.380
Ventriloquism?

12:14.380 --> 12:16.630
A similar trick you performed before?

12:18.380 --> 12:20.550
Words which shouldn't be able to reach their destination...

12:23.220 --> 12:24.600
A letter?

12:24.600 --> 12:25.980
A Shigofumi.

12:26.770 --> 12:29.480
A letter from the world of the departed.

12:31.150 --> 12:32.900
World of the departed?

12:32.900 --> 12:34.780
Is this a cursed letter?

12:35.400 --> 12:38.530
The sender is Machiya Shouta.

12:39.740 --> 12:45.580
Shigofumis contain the final
sentiments of people who have lost everything.

12:46.330 --> 12:48.710
It's your responsibility to accept it.

12:49.160 --> 12:50.460
What's that supposed to mean?

12:50.750 --> 12:53.040
Are you trying to make me feel guilty for my sins?

12:53.040 --> 12:54.420
Blackmail?

12:54.420 --> 12:56.800
I'm sorry, but I have no money.

12:57.340 --> 12:58.590
It matters not.

12:59.630 --> 13:03.800
It matters not to me whether someone lives or dies.

13:04.470 --> 13:06.430
People will die.

13:06.430 --> 13:08.810
It's either sooner or later.

13:09.770 --> 13:13.020
If there is a meaning behind it...

13:14.770 --> 13:16.900
then it's how a person dies.

13:21.820 --> 13:24.490
There's no one here right now.

13:42.050 --> 13:45.720
If I pull the trigger here, you will die.

13:46.600 --> 13:48.220
Consider it carefully.

13:48.220 --> 13:50.020
You're a moment away from losing your life.

13:50.850 --> 13:54.770
Your body, your assets, your existence will all disappear.

13:55.520 --> 13:57.150
You must still have attachments left.

13:57.150 --> 13:59.110
You must still have regrets.

14:04.530 --> 14:07.790
Regrets...?

14:12.120 --> 14:15.790
I didn't think you'd use it.

14:15.790 --> 14:16.590
Yeah.

14:24.220 --> 14:27.760
This is just another Shigofumi now.

14:28.560 --> 14:30.720
The seats are all vacant.

14:31.020 --> 14:34.600
Okay, let's take those seats over there then?

14:34.600 --> 14:37.270
See? It's better to get on here at
Kamome Station, where the train is empty.

14:37.270 --> 14:38.360
Yep.

14:38.940 --> 14:42.110
Wasn't there a strangely dressed girl here?

14:42.110 --> 14:43.610
No, there wasn't.

14:43.610 --> 14:47.070
That's odd. She was carrying a staff.

14:47.070 --> 14:49.030
She was with us earlier, wasn't she?

14:49.030 --> 14:51.120
She can see spirits.

14:51.120 --> 14:52.450
Seriously?

15:14.390 --> 15:18.480
That's odd. There's one missing.

15:21.570 --> 15:22.990
Be careful.

15:22.990 --> 15:24.860
She's very pure-hearted.

15:24.860 --> 15:25.400
Huh?

15:26.070 --> 15:32.040
You have nothing to fear from criminals who are only
concerned with the gains and losses of money and status.

15:33.870 --> 15:37.830
The most fearsome ones are the pure-hearted criminals.

15:45.130 --> 15:46.340
Are you so stupid?

15:46.340 --> 15:47.380
Are you so stupid?

15:47.380 --> 15:48.430
Are you so stupid?

15:48.430 --> 15:50.010
Are you so stupid?

15:54.560 --> 15:56.350
<i>Dear beloved Ayase,</i>

15:57.640 --> 16:02.360
<i>Ayase, you must be surprised to
receive something like this out of the blue.</i>

16:03.280 --> 16:05.990
<i>I thought for quite a long time about what to write.</i>

16:06.490 --> 16:08.410
<i>I thought hard, but...</i>

16:08.820 --> 16:11.780
<i>Sorry for not noticing.</i>

16:13.080 --> 16:15.580
<i>I was only thinking about myself.</i>

16:16.040 --> 16:20.170
<i>I never considered what type of girl you were.</i>

16:19.040 --> 16:19.080
Promise

16:19.040 --> 16:19.080
The rocket will
successfully fly!!

16:20.670 --> 16:24.000
<i>In spite of that, you believed in my rocket.</i>

16:24.380 --> 16:25.460
<i>Thank you.</i>

16:25.760 --> 16:27.220
Why are you so stupid?

16:27.800 --> 16:29.760
I killed you!

16:29.760 --> 16:32.640
I'm the one who killed you.

16:33.810 --> 16:37.350
<i>You</i> are the one who believed in me.

16:51.280 --> 16:53.950
Shouta, did you know?

16:53.950 --> 16:57.500
Shouta, I really hated you.

17:02.040 --> 17:04.920
You were always talking about your dreams.

17:05.380 --> 17:11.050
The stories about me like being the student
council president or learning the piano were all lies.

17:11.720 --> 17:15.760
What I saw in the same building was just the dark ceiling.

17:17.390 --> 17:20.770
What I saw were nightmares.

17:25.070 --> 17:29.780
But, Shouta, you were always looking
into the never-ending skies from the rooftop.

17:41.750 --> 17:43.000
Shouta...

17:46.460 --> 17:50.510
I told you that I believed in your rocket, didn't I?

17:51.800 --> 17:55.640
But, what I wanted to believe in wasn't the rocket.

17:52.470 --> 17:52.510
Asuna & Miku

17:55.640 --> 17:57.350
It was our futures.

17:57.850 --> 18:02.310
If the rocket flew, I believed that
it would open a new tomorrow for us.

18:02.770 --> 18:04.690
What a worthless wish.

18:13.200 --> 18:15.320
Hello? This is Nojima.

18:15.320 --> 18:18.330
My location is the bowling centre currently under redevelopment...

18:30.090 --> 18:32.590
From one to fifty...

18:34.050 --> 18:35.800
All checked.

18:53.820 --> 18:57.410
<i>Be careful. This girl is pure-hearted.</i>

18:57.410 --> 18:58.490
Noji-san.

19:03.040 --> 19:05.000
Countdown commenced.

19:15.300 --> 19:17.680
I've been searching for you, Asuna-chan.

19:18.180 --> 19:20.850
This was the Blue Skies Theme Park, wasn't it?

19:20.850 --> 19:23.640
I used to bring my son here often in the past.

19:24.060 --> 19:25.850
Well, never mind that.

19:25.850 --> 19:28.230
This is private property.

19:28.610 --> 19:30.570
Although, I'm in here too.

19:30.570 --> 19:32.570
It's a problem, isn't it?

19:34.360 --> 19:35.780
What a strong wind.

19:35.780 --> 19:38.200
You're going to catch a cold if you stay here.

19:41.030 --> 19:43.200
Let's get out of here for now.

19:43.200 --> 19:44.330
I'm sure Miku-chan is worried...

19:44.330 --> 19:45.290
No!

19:51.840 --> 19:52.590
Asuna & Miku

19:51.920 --> 19:52.000
Shouta

19:54.760 --> 19:57.430
Shouta, is this enough...?

20:12.770 --> 20:13.940
Asuna-chan...

20:28.170 --> 20:30.920
Th-This is...

20:30.920 --> 20:32.920
Give it your all, Shouta!

21:03.410 --> 21:05.450
Can you see it, Shouta?

21:06.120 --> 21:10.370
I'm sure you're in heaven because you're a good person.

21:10.920 --> 21:14.170
As for me, I'll probably go to hell.

21:15.630 --> 21:19.380
I hope your rocket reaches its destination.

21:25.010 --> 21:26.680
Hello!

21:28.810 --> 21:30.810
You've got mail!

21:35.190 --> 21:36.530
A letter?

21:36.530 --> 21:37.570
Yeah.

21:37.570 --> 21:39.570
A slightly unusual letter.

21:40.780 --> 21:41.280
But...

21:43.530 --> 21:45.200
But, this contains...

21:46.490 --> 21:50.870
the purest and most beautiful sentiments in the world.

21:51.250 --> 21:56.090
Shigofumi

21:51.250 --> 21:56.090
Episode Two

21:51.250 --> 21:56.090
Rocket

23:27.050 --> 23:28.350
The same rooftop.

23:28.970 --> 23:30.680
The same friends.

23:31.310 --> 23:35.640
Stepping into the same life everyday is unexpectedly easy.

23:36.480 --> 23:38.560
Next time on Shigofumi:

23:39.060 --> 23:40.360
Friends.

23:39.400 --> 23:41.400
Shigofumi

23:39.400 --> 23:41.400
Episode Three

23:39.400 --> 23:41.400
Friends
